{{!--
  The dossier: the creator's left-hand column, and the answer to two problems that used to be
  solved separately and badly.

  It is the character sheet filling up in front of the player — portrait, name, class line, the six
  ability plates — and it is *also* the step navigation. Those were two objects before: a stepper
  across the top that showed ticks but no values, and a Review step at the very end that was the
  only place to see what you had actually chosen. Four steps in, a player could not answer "what
  species did I take?" without navigating away and losing their place.

  Merging them means a step line carries its own answer. `summary` is the short line each step
  module already produced for the old stepper (class-step.mjs summary(), etc.) — it was being
  rendered as a tooltip. Here it is the value on the line, so the roll reads as a sheet:

      CLASS        Fighter · 15 / 14 / 13 / 10 / 12 / 8   ✔
      SPECIES      —                                      to do
      BACKGROUND   —                                      (dim: not reachable yet)

  State is carried by `dossier.steps[]`, built by the shell's #dossierContext():
    active     – the step on screen                complete  – done (brass tick)
    reachable  – everything before it is done, so the line is clickable
    applicable – shown but struck (e.g. Spells for a non-caster)
  Clicking a line fires data-action="goto" with its index, exactly as the old stepper did.

  Nothing here takes input. The dossier is strictly a readout; every control that *sets* one of
  these values lives on the work surface to its right. That rule is why the ability plates below
  are plates and not steppers.
--}}
<aside class="creator-dossier" aria-label="{{localize 'sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.aria'}}">

  {{!-- Identity. The portrait is whatever the Details step has set; until then it is the
        system's mystery-man, which reads as an empty frame rather than a broken image. --}}
  <div class="creator-dossier-ident">
    <div class="creator-dossier-plate">
      <img src="{{dossier.portrait}}" alt="">
    </div>
    <div class="creator-dossier-names">
      <p class="creator-dossier-name {{#unless dossier.name}}is-unset{{/unless}}">
        {{#if dossier.name}}{{dossier.name}}{{else}}{{localize "sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.unnamed"}}{{/if}}
      </p>
      <p class="creator-dossier-sub">
        {{#if dossier.className}}
        {{localize "sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.levelClass" level=dossier.level class=dossier.className}}
        {{else}}
        {{localize "sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.noClass"}}
        {{/if}}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {{!-- The six scores, as a readout. `set` is false until the ability step has produced a
        complete set, so the plates read as blanks on the sheet rather than as a rolled 8/8/8/8/8/8
        the player never chose. The bonus corner appears only where an origin actually adds one. --}}
  <ul class="creator-dossier-scores">
    {{#each dossier.abilities}}
    <li class="creator-dossier-score {{#unless ../dossier.abilitiesSet}}is-unset{{/unless}}">
      <span class="creator-dossier-abbr">{{abbr}}</span>
      <span class="creator-dossier-value">{{#if ../dossier.abilitiesSet}}{{value}}{{else}}&mdash;{{/if}}</span>
      <span class="creator-dossier-mod">{{#if ../dossier.abilitiesSet}}{{modifier}}{{/if}}</span>
      {{#if bonus}}<span class="creator-dossier-bonus" data-tooltip="{{bonusTip}}">{{bonus}}</span>{{/if}}
    </li>
    {{/each}}
  </ul>

  {{!-- The roll: every step, with its value and its state. This is the navigation — so it is a
        <nav>, giving screen-reader and keyboard users a landmark to jump straight to it. The
        surrounding <aside> covers the whole dossier, most of which is readout; without this the
        step list had no landmark of its own and had to be found by tabbing. --}}
  <nav aria-labelledby="creator-dossier-roll-heading">
  <h2 class="creator-dossier-heading" id="creator-dossier-roll-heading">{{localize "sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.roll"}}</h2>
  <ol class="creator-dossier-roll">
    {{#each dossier.steps}}
    <li>
      <button type="button"
              class="creator-dossier-line {{#if active}}is-active{{/if}} {{#if complete}}is-complete{{/if}} {{#unless applicable}}is-skipped{{/unless}} {{#if open}}is-open{{/if}}"
              data-action="goto" data-index="{{index}}"
              {{#unless reachable}}disabled{{/unless}}
              {{#if active}}aria-current="step"{{/if}}>
        <span class="creator-dossier-key">{{label}}</span>
        {{!-- The value column is about 150px, so a long name (a species from a third-party
              module, a custom background) still runs past the ellipsis. The summaries are
              short by design now — see class-step.mjs summary() — but "short by design" is a
              promise about our own steps, not about the compendium, so the full text is on
              the element as a tooltip whenever there is any. --}}
        <span class="creator-dossier-value-line" {{#if summary}}data-tooltip="{{summary}}"{{/if}}>
          {{#if summary}}{{summary}}
          {{else if applicable}}&mdash;
          {{else}}{{localize "sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.notApplicable"}}{{/if}}
        </span>
        {{!-- State is never carried by colour alone: complete gets a tick, outstanding gets a
              word. `open` is set only where the player can actually act — a reachable,
              applicable, unfinished step — so the teal never marks something they can't do
              anything about yet. --}}
        {{#if complete}}<i class="creator-dossier-tick fa-solid fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/if}}
        {{#if open}}<span class="creator-dossier-todo">{{localize "sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.todo"}}</span>{{/if}}
      </button>
    </li>
    {{/each}}
  </ol>
  </nav>
</aside>
